orkItemDatabase.md","line":31},{"title":"Get-PSWorkItemPreference","target":"docs/Get-PSWorkItemPreference.md","line":32},{"title":"Get-PSWorkItemReport","target":"docs/Get-PSWorkItemReport.md","line":33},{"title":"Initialize-PSWorkItemDatabase","target":"docs/Initialize-PSWorkItemDatabase.md","line":34},{"title":"New-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/New-PSWorkItem.md","line":35},{"title":"Open-PSWorkItemConsole","target":"docs/Open-PSWorkItemConsole.md","line":36},{"title":"Open-PSWorkItemHelp","target":"docs/Open-PSWorkItemHelp.md","line":37},{"title":"Remove-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Remove-PSWorkItem.md","line":38},{"title":"Remove-PSWorkItemArchive","target":"docs/Remove-PSWorkItemArchive.md","line":39},{"title":"Remove-PSWorkItemCategory","target":"docs/Remove-PSWorkItemCategory.md","line":40},{"title":"Set-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Set-PSWorkItem.md","line":41},{"title":"Set-PSWorkItemCategory","target":"docs/Set-PSWorkItemCategory.md","line":42},{"title":"Update-PSWorkItemDatabase","target":"docs/Update-PSWorkItemDatabase.md","line":43},{"title":"Update-PSWorkItemPreference","target":"docs/Update-PSWorkItemPreference.md","line":44},{"title":"Get-PSWorkItem","target":"images/get-psworkitem.png","line":213,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Get-PSWorkItem.md","line":217},{"title":"38;5;153m\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe entry will have no effect unless the category is defined in the database. The category customizations last for the duration of your PowerShell session or until the module is removed. Add your customizations to your PowerShell profile script or use `Update-PSWorkItemPreference` to save the settings to a JSON file under $HOME.\r\n\r\n> Note that when you view the hashtable, you won't see any values because the escape sequences are non-printable.\r\n\r\n![Colorized Categories","target":"images/psworkitemcategory.png","line":233},{"title":"Set-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Set-PSWorkItem.md","line":246},{"title":"Complete-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Complete-PSWorkItem.md","line":273},{"title":"Remove-PSWorkItem","target":"docs/Remove-PSWorkItem.md","line":277},{"title":"Remove-PSWorkItemArchive","target":"docs/Remove-PSWorkItemArchive.md","line":285},{"title":"Get-PSWorkItemReport","target":"docs/Get-PSWorkItemReport.md","line":289},{"title":"Terminal.Gui","target":"https://github.com/gui-cs/Terminal.Gui","line":311},{"title":"Using Terminal Console Management","target":"images/psworkitemconsole.png","line":313,"embedded":true},{"title":"`Open-PSWorkItemConsole`","target":"docs\\Open-PSWorkItemConsole.md","line":315},{"title":"Add a category with the TUI console","target":"images/tui-addcategory.png","line":321,"embedded":true},{"title":"Set the category with the TUI console","target":"images/tui-setcategory.png","line":323,"embedded":true},{"title":"Get details with the TUI console","target":"images/tui-taskdetail.png","line":327,"embedded":true},{"title":"38;5;204m\r\nProject     `e[38;5;215m\r\nEvent       `e[38;5;153m\r\nTraining    `e[94m\r\nWork        `e[36m\r\nPersonal    `e[32m\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe categories are only those where you have customized an ANSI sequence. On module import, these categories will be used to populate `$PSWorkItemCategory.` If you make any changes to your preference, re-run `Update-PSWorkItemPreference`.\r\n\r\n> You might need to manually delete the JSON preferences file if you uninstall the module.\r\n\r\n## Database Backup\r\n\r\nThis module has no specific commands for backing up or restoring a database file. But you can use the `Export-MySQLiteDB` command to export the PSWorkItem database file to a JSON file.\r\n\r\n```powershell\r\nExport-MySQLiteDB -path $PSWorkItemPath -Destination d:\\backups\\pwi.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nUse `Import-MySQLiteDB` to import the file and rebuild the database file. When restoring a database file, you should restore the file to a new location, verify the database, and then copy the file to `$PSWorkItemPath`.\r\n\r\n## Database Sample\r\n\r\nA sample database has been created in the module's Samples directory. You can specify the path to the sample database or copy it to `$PSWorkItemPath` to try the module out. Note that it is very likely that many of the tasks will be flagged as overdue by the time you view the database.\r\n\r\nIf you copy the sample to `$PSWorkItemPath`, delete the file before creating your database file.\r\n\r\n## Reminders and Alerts\r\n\r\nI have received requests and questions about integrating a reminder or alert system. This module does not have any built-in features for this. You could use a scheduled task or a PowerShell script to query the database for tasks due within a certain time frame and then send an email or other alert. I am reluctant to include this feature because I have no way of knowing how **you** would want to be alerted or what kind of alert you would want. That said, here are some ways you could implement this feature.\r\n\r\n### Send-MailKitMessage\r\n\r\nI've started using [Send-MailKitMessage","target":"https://github.com/austineric/Send-MailKitMessage","line":362},{"title":"void","target":"$html.table.tr[$i].Attributes.Append($class","line":460},{"title":"void","target":"$html.table.tr[$i].Attributes.Append($class","line":464},{"title":"BurntToast","target":"https://github.com/Windos/BurntToast","line":516},{"title":"void","target":"$PSBoundParameters.remove('At'","line":648},{"title":"void","target":"$PSBoundParameters.remove('Name'","line":649},{"title":"Discussion section","target":"https://github.com/jdhitsolutions/PSWorkItem/discussions","line":711},{"title":"Update-PSWorkItemDatabase","target":"docs/Update-PSWorkItemDatabase.md","line":717},{"title":"class definitions","target":"PSWorkItem.psm1","line":723},{"title":"submit it as an Issue","target":"https://github.com/jdhitsolutions/PSWorkItem/issues","line":745}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
